{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And they shall eat them, that by which atonement was made.</b> That is, by virtue of their being its owners, and not by virtue of their being priests. And this is what the verse says <b>אֲשֶׁר כֻּפַּר בָּהֶם</b> — for the eating of shelamim by the owners activates the atonement, and they are forbidden even to Moshe, even though he eats the breast, which is forbidden to Aharon."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:34:29.085074063Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}